    <div>
      Our institutions are failing and the future feels closed – yet hope is still possible. <b>No Fixed Ground</b> asks how to
      live a good life, and how to build a better society, when nothing is certain.
    </div>

    <div>
      The answer begins with an admission – no amount of searching will find certainty. What follows isn't despair but
      freedom: the foundations below us were never discovered, only chosen, so we're free to choose our own. In that
      freedom hope begins.
    </div>

    <div>
      An honest essay about standing steady on shifting ground.
    </div>


